  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "",
    "plain": "The parent proof `bezout-identity-oq-04-oq-01` formalized linear Diophantine systems using Smith normal form, but had to axiomatize some results. The question is whether Mathlib's `Matrix.smithNormalForm` (or equivalent PID-module theory) already provides the machinery to turn those axioms into theorems.",
